```
CertWatch - Splunk searches. Events arrive via HEC with sourcetype "certwatch:finding".
If fields are not auto-extracted, add to props.conf:
    [certwatch:finding]
    KV_MODE = json
```

```
1) ALERT (run every 5 min, trigger if results > 0): new HIGH / CRITICAL impersonation domains
```
index=security sourcetype="certwatch:finding" severity IN ("HIGH","CRITICAL") earliest=-5m
| stats latest(_time) as last_seen max(score) as score
        values(reasons{}) as reasons values(ips{}) as ips values(issuer) as issuer
        by domain target
| sort - score

```
2) HUNT: impersonation domains that already resolve in DNS (most likely live phishing infrastructure)
```
index=security sourcetype="certwatch:finding" resolved=true earliest=-24h
| stats max(score) as score values(ips{}) as ips by domain target
| sort - score

```
3) REPORT: daily summary by brand and severity
```
index=security sourcetype="certwatch:finding" earliest=-24h@h
| timechart span=1h count by severity

```
4) HUNT: which CAs are issuing certificates for look-alike domains
```
index=security sourcetype="certwatch:finding" earliest=-30d
| stats count dc(domain) as unique_domains by issuer
| sort - count
